    },
    {
      "path": "app/services/bag_search_service.py",
      "content": "Consistency asymmetry within the new multi-member predicates: `nvidia_original` and `self_built_original` both exclude slice bags via `~_scene_slice_pred()`, but `scene_original` does not. Meanwhile the Python label side (`data_kind_context`) gives slice priority over everything else (an ORIGINAL bag that appears as a derivation child is labelled only `scene_slice`), and the shared priority comment says rule 1 (子包) wins. Such a bag would therefore show a `scene_slice` label yet still be returned by the `scene_original` filter — the exact filter/label divergence OCR C6 tries to remove. If the priority is meant to be single-sourced, consider `and_(BagRecord.bag_role == \"ORIGINAL\", ~_scene_slice_pred(), _scene_basis_pred())` to mirror the sibling predicates.",
      "existing_code": "    if kind == \"scene_original\":\n        return and_(BagRecord.bag_role == \"ORIGINAL\", _scene_basis_pred())",
